Description: read-only diagnostics for NVIDIA driver and CUDA setups
 gpu-doctor finds the common reasons an NVIDIA GPU or CUDA does not work on
 Ubuntu: no driver package, the kernel module not loaded, no module built for
 the running kernel after a kernel upgrade, missing kernel headers for DKMS,
 the nouveau driver holding the GPU, Secure Boot rejecting an unsigned module,
 a mismatch between the loaded module and the userspace libraries, and a CUDA
 toolkit that is too new for the driver.
 .
 Each problem is explained in plain language together with the exact commands
 that fix it. The tool never changes the system. Output is available as
 coloured text, as JSON with a documented schema, and as a redacted report
 for bug trackers and forums.
